 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Drawing is really accessible without talent. It' like riding bike or learning to cook. Are you wanting to sketch what you see, or mind maps and character designs? Start with simple lines. Pick an object in the room and draw it from lot of angles. It' a good warm up, and you' see how lines change. Rough and rough drawing. Rough is quick and messy, usually done on paper that's almost torn. Rough drawing is the finished product. Try different tools. Sharp pencils hurt at first. Pens and brushes feel completely different. Also, try different paper. Rough paper absorbs the lead quickly, smooth paper lasts much longer but feels different.",
